WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.027
Class action guide.

00:00:01.977 --> 00:00:03.965
How to join or file.

00:00:03.965 --> 00:00:11.375
This page documents active and potential class action lawsuits related to the institutional failures documented across TENET5.

00:00:11.375 --> 00:00:16.590
Class actions allow large groups of affected citizens to pursue legal remedies collectively.

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:22.534
When individual lawsuits are impractical, class actions pool resources and legal representation.

00:00:22.534 --> 00:00:32.829
This page covers: active class actions you can join, potential class actions that could be filed, how section 504 private prosecution works, and practical steps for participation.

00:00:32.829 --> 00:00:35.136
This is not legal advice.

00:00:35.136 --> 00:00:38.181
Consult a lawyer for your specific situation.

00:00:38.181 --> 00:00:40.704
Legal action is the final tool.

00:00:40.704 --> 00:00:45.022
Every other accountability mechanism documented on this site has failed.

00:00:45.022 --> 00:00:47.624
Oversight bodies can't enforce.

00:00:47.624 --> 00:00:49.590
Courts rule too late.

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:51.534
The Crown is immune.

00:00:51.534 --> 00:00:53.806
Whistleblowers are destroyed.

00:00:53.806 --> 00:00:55.897
Media is captured.

00:00:55.897 --> 00:01:02.579
Section 504 private prosecution and class actions are the mechanisms that bypass the captured system entirely.

00:01:02.579 --> 00:01:09.090
They allow citizens to pursue justice directly through the courts — bypassing the government agencies that refuse to act.

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:11.874
This guide provides the starting points.

00:01:11.874 --> 00:01:14.727
Consult a lawyer for specific advice.

00:01:14.727 --> 00:01:20.068
The evidence documented across 237 pages on this site is the foundation.
